+// The value union the storage and every GL boundary carry. Each built-in interface already extends
+// PbrExtension, so this accepts exactly the same values as PbrExtension -- including arbitrary vendor
+// extensions, through the open arm -- while naming the built-ins as redundant arms beside it. That is
+// what lets a registration read its own concrete fields from a declared arm instead of asserting them
+// back out of the open base, which the emitter cannot do because it flattens interface heritage into
+// independent owners.
+export type PbrExtensionValue =
+  | PbrExtension
+  | AnisotropyPbrExtension
+  | ClearcoatPbrExtension
+  | IridescencePbrExtension
+  | SheenPbrExtension
+  | SpecularPbrExtension
+  | TransmissionVolumePbrExtension
+  | WrappedDiffusePbrExtension;
